# Tailwind CSS Utility-First Excellence

## Core Utility-First Philosophy

- **Compose utilities directly in markup** — avoid custom CSS unless using `@apply` for repeated patterns
- **Mobile-first breakpoints** — unprefixed utilities apply to all sizes; prefix with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, `2xl:` to override upward
- **Extract components, not utilities** — when the same utility group repeats 3+ times, extract a component, not a CSS class
- **No premature abstraction** — resist moving utilities to `@apply` until duplication is proven

```tsx
// ✅ Compose utilities directly
<button className="rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm hover:bg-blue-500 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-blue-600">
  Save changes
</button>

// ❌ Avoid inventing CSS class names for one-off styles
// .my-special-button { @apply rounded-lg bg-blue-600 ... }
```

## Responsive Design Patterns

```tsx
// ✅ Mobile-first: base → sm → md → lg → xl
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4">
  {items.map((item) => (
    <Card key={item.id} {...item} />
  ))}
</div>

// ✅ Responsive typography
<h1 className="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">
  Page heading
</h1>

// ✅ Responsive visibility
<nav className="hidden lg:flex lg:gap-x-6">
  {/* Desktop nav — hidden below lg */}
</nav>
<button className="lg:hidden" aria-label="Open menu">
  {/* Mobile hamburger — hidden at lg and above */}
</button>

// ✅ Responsive spacing and layout
<aside className="w-full lg:w-64 lg:shrink-0">
  Sidebar
</aside>
<main className="min-w-0 flex-1">
  Content
</main>
```

## Dark Mode

Configure `darkMode: 'class'` in `tailwind.config.ts` to toggle dark mode via a CSS class on `<html>`.

```tsx
// ✅ Pair light and dark utilities with dark: prefix
<div className="bg-white text-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
  <h2 className="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">Heading</h2>
  <p className="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Body text</p>
</div>

// ✅ Dark mode borders and shadows
<div className="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm dark:border-gray-700 dark:shadow-gray-900/50">
  Card content
</div>

// ✅ Dark mode interactive states
<button className="bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-500 dark:bg-indigo-500 dark:hover:bg-indigo-400">
  Action
</button>
```

## Component Extraction with @apply

Use `@apply` only when a utility group is truly reused across unrelated files and a React/Vue component isn't the right abstraction (e.g., prose styles, base form inputs reset).

```css
/* ✅ Base input reset — shared across many unrelated forms */
@layer components {
  .input-base {
    @apply w-full rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm
           placeholder-gray-400 shadow-sm
           focus:border-indigo-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-indigo-500
           dark:border-gray-600 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    @apply inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-indigo-600
           px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm
           hover:bg-indigo-500
           focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-indigo-600
           disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50;
  }
}
```

```tsx
{/* ✅ Use the abstracted classes */}
<input type="email" className="input-base" placeholder="you@example.com" />
<button className="btn-primary" disabled={loading}>
  {loading ? 'Saving…' : 'Save'}
</button>
```

## Arbitrary Values

Use `[]` syntax for one-off values that fall outside the design scale.

```tsx
// ✅ Arbitrary pixel/rem values when design requires exact spec
<div className="h-[560px] w-[calc(100%-2rem)]">
  Hero section
</div>

// ✅ Arbitrary colors (prefer extending config for repeated colors)
<span className="text-[#E63946]">Warning text</span>

// ✅ Arbitrary grid template
<div className="grid grid-cols-[1fr_2fr_1fr] gap-6">
  <aside />
  <main />
  <aside />
</div>

// ✅ Arbitrary CSS properties via []
<div className="[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,black,transparent)]">
  Fade out content
</div>
```

## Tailwind Config Customization

Extend the default theme — never replace it — to add brand tokens while keeping all Tailwind defaults available.

```typescript
// ✅ tailwind.config.ts
import type { Config } from 'tailwindcss'

const config: Config = {
  content: ['./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,html}'],
  darkMode: 'class',
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        brand: {
          50: '#eff6ff',
          500: '#3b82f6',
          600: '#2563eb',
          700: '#1d4ed8',
          900: '#1e3a5f',
        },
      },
      fontFamily: {
        sans: ['Inter var', 'ui-sans-serif', 'system-ui'],
        mono: ['JetBrains Mono', 'ui-monospace'],
      },
      borderRadius: {
        '4xl': '2rem',
      },
      animation: {
        'fade-in': 'fadeIn 0.2s ease-in-out',
        'slide-up': 'slideUp 0.3s ease-out',
      },
      keyframes: {
        fadeIn: { from: { opacity: '0' }, to: { opacity: '1' } },
        slideUp: { from: { transform: 'translateY(8px)', opacity: '0' }, to: { transform: 'translateY(0)', opacity: '1' } },
      },
    },
  },
  plugins: [
    require('@tailwindcss/forms'),
    require('@tailwindcss/typography'),
  ],
}

export default config
```

## State and Group Variants

```tsx
// ✅ group — style children based on parent hover/focus
<a href="#" className="group flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg p-3 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-800">
  <span className="text-gray-400 group-hover:text-indigo-600">
    <Icon />
  </span>
  <span className="font-medium text-gray-700 group-hover:text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-300">
    Dashboard
  </span>
</a>

// ✅ peer — style siblings based on sibling state (e.g. floating label)
<div className="relative">
  <input
    id="email"
    type="email"
    placeholder=" "
    className="peer block w-full rounded-md border border-gray-300 px-3 pb-2 pt-5 text-sm
               focus:border-indigo-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-indigo-500"
  />
  <label
    htmlFor="email"
    className="absolute left-3 top-2 text-xs text-gray-500 transition-all
               peer-placeholder-shown:top-4 peer-placeholder-shown:text-sm
               peer-focus:top-2 peer-focus:text-xs peer-focus:text-indigo-600"
  >
    Email
  </label>
</div>

// ✅ has — style parent when child matches (Tailwind v3.4+)
<label className="flex cursor-pointer gap-2 has-[:checked]:text-indigo-600">
  <input type="checkbox" className="accent-indigo-600" />
  Subscribe to newsletter
</label>
```

