## Key Rules

- Run `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` to auto-sort class lists — never sort by hand
- Avoid mixing Tailwind utilities with global CSS on the same element
- Use `clsx` or `cva` (class-variance-authority) for conditional and variant-based class composition, not string interpolation
- Purge is automatic when `content` paths in `tailwind.config.ts` cover all template files — verify the paths if classes go missing in production
- Do **not** use string interpolation to build class names (`bg-${color}-600`) — Tailwind's scanner is regex-based and won't detect dynamically constructed strings; use a complete-class lookup object instead

```tsx
// ❌ Dynamic string interpolation — class won't be detected
<div className={`bg-${status}-600`} />

// ✅ Lookup object — all classes are statically present in source
const statusClass = {
  success: 'bg-green-600',
  error: 'bg-red-600',
  warning: 'bg-yellow-600',
} as const

<div className={statusClass[status]} />
```
